#
# Whether a select fires its action (pivot_rules.h PV4), in Sutra. A plain
# action (held 0) fires on its select. A held action (held 1: pay, grant,
# trash) fires only when a second select on the confirm target followed
# (confirm 1); its first select never fires it. Both are one-digit flags:
# 2 to 9 is no flag and never yes, and a negative does not fit: refused.
record dwell-fires
  held: 9
  confirm: 9
procedure
  answer held = 0 or held = 1 and confirm = 1
